---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeaderV7.astro";
import "../styles/global-v7.css";
import "../styles/pilot-families.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>First 5 Pilot Families | HarborNavi</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Apply for HarborNavi's two-week Pilot Families program. Selected families receive a new device, lifetime subscription-free access, and a $500 completion bonus." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" sizes="512x512" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://harbornavi.com/pilot-families" />
  </head>
  <body class="pilot-page" data-route="pilot-families">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <section class="pilot-hero" aria-labelledby="pilot-title">
        <img src="/assets/home-v6-pilot-families-v1.png" alt="A family trying HarborNavi together during an early pilot experience" width="1801" height="873" fetchpriority="high" />
        <div class="pilot-hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="pilot-hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">HarborNavi Pilot Program</p>
          <h1 id="pilot-title">Be One of the First 5 Pilot Families</h1>
          <p>Join a two-week, at-home pilot. Receive a new HarborNavi, lifetime subscription-free access, and a $500 completion bonus.</p>
          <a class="pilot-primary" href="#waitlist">Apply to Join <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="pilot-intro section-shell" aria-labelledby="pilot-intro-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Five homes. Real feedback.</p>
          <h2 id="pilot-intro-title">Help us build HarborNavi around the way families actually live.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Selected households will use HarborNavi for two weeks with their existing smart-home setup, share practical feedback, and help us improve the experience before a wider release.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pilot-details section-shell" aria-label="Pilot family benefits">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>A new HarborNavi</h3>
          <p>Each selected family receives a brand-new HarborNavi device for the pilot and keeps it after completing the program.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>No subscription fees, for life</h3>
          <p>Your pilot device includes lifetime subscription-free access to the HarborNavi product experience.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>$500 completion bonus</h3>
          <p>Each of the first five pilot families can receive an additional $500 after completing the agreed pilot milestones.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="pilot-commitment section-shell" aria-labelledby="commitment-title">
        <div class="pilot-commitment-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A focused two-week pilot</p>
          <h2 id="commitment-title">Use HarborNavi in real life, then show us what worked.</h2>
          <p>The pilot is designed to be useful without becoming a second job. Final scheduling, reward milestones, and participation terms are shared before a selected family confirms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pilot-commitment-grid">
          <article>
            <p class="eyebrow">What pilot families do</p>
            <h3>Install, use, and document the experience.</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Install HarborNavi with guided setup support.</li>
              <li>Use it in normal household routines for two weeks.</li>
              <li>Share structured feedback through short check-ins.</li>
              <li>Record one or two short vlogs about the experience.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article>
            <p class="eyebrow">Who we are looking for</p>
            <h3>Families ready to give practical, honest feedback.</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A stable home Wi-Fi connection.</li>
              <li>At least one compatible camera or Home Assistant device.</li>
              <li>An adult who can participate in setup and feedback sessions.</li>
              <li>Comfort sharing what works, what is confusing, and what should change.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="pilot-privacy section-shell" aria-labelledby="pilot-privacy-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p>
          <h2 id="pilot-privacy-title">Your home data stays in your home.</h2>
          <p>HarborNavi does not collect your household's camera footage, device credentials, or private home timeline as part of the pilot. Home data is processed locally on HarborNavi.</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Local processing</strong><span>Camera events, device context, and home memories are handled on the HarborNavi device.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Minimal application data</strong><span>We ask only for contact information and a high-level device summary during selection.</span></li>
          <li><strong>You control sharing</strong><span>You decide what feedback, vlog footage, and optional diagnostics to share with the team.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pilot-process section-shell" aria-labelledby="process-title">
        <div class="pilot-process-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">How selection works</p>
          <h2 id="process-title">A short application, followed by a conversation.</h2>
          <p>We will review setup compatibility, availability, and the kind of feedback each applicant hopes to contribute. Applying does not guarantee selection or create a marketing subscription.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Apply</strong><span>Tell us about your household and current setup.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Review</strong><span>The HarborNavi team reviews applications for pilot fit.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Confirm</strong><span>Selected families receive the final schedule, milestones, reward terms, and participation agreement before deciding.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <aside>
          <p class="eyebrow">Before you decide</p>
          <h3>Clear terms before installation.</h3>
          <p>Selected families receive the final schedule, device terms, completion milestones, $500 bonus terms, and participation agreement before committing.</p>
          <a href="#pilot-faq">Read the pilot FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section id="pilot-faq" class="pilot-faq section-shell" aria-labelledby="pilot-faq-title">
        <div class="pilot-faq-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Pilot FAQ</p>
          <h2 id="pilot-faq-title">What families ask before joining.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="pilot-faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What's expected of pilot testers?</summary>
            <p>Install HarborNavi with guided support, use it in your normal household routines for two weeks, complete short feedback check-ins, and record one or two short vlogs about the experience.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What equipment do I need?</summary>
            <p>You need stable Wi-Fi and at least one compatible camera or Home Assistant device. We will confirm compatibility before selection is final.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How long is the pilot program?</summary>
            <p>The active home-use period is two weeks, plus a short setup session and final feedback check-in.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do I get to keep the device?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Families that complete the pilot keep their HarborNavi device.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens after the pilot?</summary>
            <p>You keep the HarborNavi device and receive lifetime subscription-free access for that pilot device. Families that complete the agreed milestones can also receive the $500 completion bonus.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="waitlist" class="pilot-application section-shell" aria-labelledby="application-title">
        <div class="pilot-application-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Pilot application</p>
          <h2 id="application-title">Apply for the HarborNavi pilot.</h2>
          <p>Six quick questions help us confirm compatibility and select a varied first group. A submitted application is not a guarantee of selection.</p>
        </div>
        <form data-pilot-form>
          <label> Name <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="120" required /> </label>
          <label> Email <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254" required /> </label>
          <label> ZIP Code <input type="text" name="zip_code" autocomplete="postal-code" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?" maxlength="10" required /> </label>
          <label class="full-field"> What smart devices do you currently use? <textarea name="smart_devices" rows="4" maxlength="1200" required></textarea> </label>
          <label class="full-field"> Why are you interested? <textarea name="interest_reason" rows="4" maxlength="1200" required></textarea> </label>
          <label class="full-field"> How did you hear about us?
            <select name="referral_source" required>
              <option value="">Select one</option>
              <option value="search">Search</option>
              <option value="social">Social media</option>
              <option value="friend-family">Friend or family</option>
              <option value="kickstarter">Kickstarter</option>
              <option value="community-event">Community or event</option>
              <option value="other">Other</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <input class="pilot-honeypot" type="text" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
          <p class="pilot-form-note full-field">By submitting, you are applying only to the pilot program. This does not subscribe you to marketing email. See <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.</p>
          <p class="pilot-form-message full-field" data-pilot-message aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
          <button class="pilot-primary full-field" type="submit">Submit application <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><span>HarborNavi</span><a href="/home-v7">Home</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></footer>

    <script is:inline>
      const pilotForm = document.querySelector("[data-pilot-form]");
      const pilotMessage = document.querySelector("[data-pilot-message]");
      pilotForm?.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        const button = pilotForm.querySelector("button[type='submit']");
        const data = new FormData(pilotForm);
        button.disabled = true;
        pilotMessage.hidden = true;
        try {
          const response = await fetch("/api/pilot-application", {
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "content-type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(data.entries()))
          });
          const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
          if (!response.ok) throw new Error(body.error || "We could not submit your application.");
          pilotForm.reset();
          pilotMessage.textContent = "Application received. We will contact selected families with the next steps.";
          pilotMessage.dataset.tone = "success";
        } catch (error) {
          pilotMessage.textContent = error instanceof Error ? error.message : "We could not submit your application.";
          pilotMessage.dataset.tone = "error";
        } finally {
          pilotMessage.hidden = false;
          button.disabled = false;
        }
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
